  "summary": "Both worker functions modify the same global non-atomic int counter at workers.c lines 9 and 16. The successful creation path starts both workers before either join, permitting their conflicting accesses to overlap. writer_a holds mutex while writer_b holds the separately declared second_mutex. Their critical sections therefore have no common mutex or other ordering protocol. The joins synchronize worker completion with main's subsequent read but provide no ordering between the two worker accesses. The PR directly introduces the race by switching writer_b from mutex to second_mutex. The supplied candidate_decision.max_status limits this review to probable.",
